            title: 'BrÃºs Iceland',
            subtitle: 'Card game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "BrÃºs Iceland is the Icelandic partnership version of Brus, played by four players in fixed partnerships using a 36-card stripped French deck. The game focuses on timing powerful 'beating cards', managing risk with the King of hearts, and racing your team to the scoring target.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'BrÃºs is the Icelandic version of the Danish game Brus, itself a descendant of the medieval KarnÃ¶ffel family. It took root in northern Iceland, especially the SvarfaÃ°ardalur valley and villages such as DalvÃk and GrenivÃk, where it became a staple evening and festival game.',
              },
            ],
          },
