          deckDescription: 'One 36-card stripped French deck created by removing all 2s, 3s, 4s and 5s from a standard 52-card pack, leaving six through ace in each suit. This is the traditional pack used for BrÃºs in Iceland and related KarnÃ¶ffel-family games.',
          suitDescription: 'Four French suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs). Suits share a common set of powerful beating cards, but there is no separate trump suit in Icelandic BrÃºs; trick winners are determined by the special ranking of beating cards.',
          rankDescription: 'Each suit uses ranks A, K, Q, J, 10, 9, 8, 7 and 6 for a total of 36 cards. During play, certain ranks (J, K, 8, 9, A and 6) form the beating cards that can win tricks; the remaining ranks are always non-beating cards.',
          dealPattern: 'Each player is dealt three cards from the 36-card pack; after each trick, players draw from the stock so everyone returns to three cards until the stock is exhausted.',
          bettingLimits: 'NA',
          actions: {},
          handRankingSystem: 'Standard poker hand rankings.',
          rankingSystem: '',
          useTrump: false,
